course: dictionary
lesson: 594
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The words around them, their context, show you which meaning the writer wants. «The parade marched down the avenue, past rows of tall trees.» Here the trees and the marching tell you an avenue is a wide street.
explain: Read the clue words first. In «Explore every avenue before you give up», the clue is explore. You cannot explore a street, so avenue must mean a way of trying to reach something. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Word forms can help too. In an address, «Fifth Avenue» tells you the place is a street, not a person or a building. Writers often shorten it to «Ave.», so when you see Ave. after a name, think street.
fact: «Avenue» means a wide street in a town or city, often with trees along the sides.
fact: «Avenue» can also mean a road or path lined with trees, leading to a big house.
fact: «Avenue» can mean a way of doing or reaching something, as in «explore every avenue».
fact: In addresses, «Avenue» is often written as «Ave.», as in «Fifth Avenue».
fact: The Champs-Élysées is a famous avenue in Paris, and a big military parade takes place there on 14 July.
exercise: «The parade marched down the avenue, past rows of tall trees.» What is an avenue here? | *A wide street with trees along the sides | A small garden bird | A type of boat | A kind of cake
exercise: «Explore every avenue before you give up.» What does avenue mean here? | A tall tower | *A way of trying to reach something | A wide street in a town | A type of tree
exercise: In the address «Fifth Avenue», what does Avenue tell you? | It is the sea | A river runs through it | *It is a street | It is a shop only
test: «The road to the big house was an avenue of oak trees, with branches meeting overhead.» What does avenue mean in this sentence? | An ocean | *A road lined with trees | A loud bell | A small room
test: In a written address, «Fifth Avenue» is often shortened to what? | Avn | Fif. Av | Av. Five | *Ave.
exam: «On 14 July there is a big parade on the Champs-Élysées, a famous avenue in Paris.» What is the Champs-Élysées? | A famous river in Paris | A museum | *A famous avenue in Paris | A small park
